# PizzaApp API: register, log in, and the saved pizzas.
#
# 1. Start the API with the "http" profile (http://localhost:5004) on a migrated database.
# 2. Send the requests IN ORDER, top to bottom. A request marked "# @name" keeps its response,
#    and later requests reuse the token or an id from it, e.g. {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
#
# Visual Studio: click "Send request" above a request. VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension.
# Every error has the same body: { "statusCode", "message", "errors", "traceId" }

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5004/api


### ─── 1. AUTH (anonymous) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Register a customer → 201 + the new user, with the Customer role.
# If "ana" already exists (you ran this file before) you get 400: skip it and log in.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "ana",
  "email": "ana@pizzaapp.local",
  "password": "Ana123!"
}

### Log in as the customer → 200 + { token, expiresAt, userName, roles }
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "ana",
  "password": "Ana123!"
}

### A second customer, for the 403 tests → 201 (or 400 if "bob" already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "bob",
  "email": "bob@pizzaapp.local",
  "password": "Bob123!"
}

### Log in as the second customer → 200
# @name bobLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "bob",
  "password": "Bob123!"
}

### Log in as the admin that the Init migration seeded → 200, roles: ["Admin"]
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Wrong password → 401 with a generic message (it doesn't reveal whether "ana" exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "ana",
  "password": "not-my-password"
}


### ─── 2. SAVED PIZZAS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a pizza → 201 + a Location header + the pizza with its new id
# @name createPizza
POST {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Margherita",
  "description": "The classic",
  "price": 7.50,
  "ingredients": ["TomatoSauce", "Mozzarella", "Basil"]
}

### Invalid pizza → 400 with every validation error in "errors"
POST {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": 0,
  "ingredients": []
}

### An ingredient we don't have → 400 (enums travel as text, unknown names are rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hawaii",
  "price": 9.00,
  "ingredients": ["TomatoSauce", "Pineapple"]
}

### My saved pizzas → 200 (a customer sees only their own)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### One pizza → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Update it → 200, with a new updatedDate
PUT {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Margherita",
  "description": "The classic, with oregano",
  "price": 8.00,
  "ingredients": ["TomatoSauce", "Mozzarella", "Basil", "Oregano"]
}

### Somebody else's pizza → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Changing somebody else's pizza → 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mine now",
  "price": 1.00,
  "ingredients": ["TomatoSauce"]
}

### Deleting somebody else's pizza → 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### The admin may see anybody's pizza → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### The admin sees everybody's saved pizzas → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Delete it → 204 (no body)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Get it again → 404 ("Pizza with id … was not found.")
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas/{{createPizza.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### No token → 401: every endpoint needs a login, except register, login and the API docs
GET {{baseUrl}}/pizzas
